# Independent review: single Pages creation POST transport

Verdict: no blocking finding in the reviewed transport scope. Exact six-file source snapshots are under source/; the diff was reviewed against base 5dd9569.

Independently checked the [GitHub Pages creation REST contract](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/pages/pages#create-a-github-pages-deployment): artifact_id, pages_build_version, environment and oidc_token are the appropriate request fields and successful creation returns HTTP 200. Requiring a 40-hex build version and a bounded exact-integer artifact ID is the repository's narrower transport profile. Reviewed create.py, the isolated worker, shared HTTP request extraction, changed HTTP fixture and README against chapter 15's durable-intent and uncertain-outcome requirements.

The public boundary validates inputs before starting a process, sends credentials on stdin, executes one isolated worker, validates the original response again, and turns worker/HTTP/parse uncertainty into CreationUnknown without retry. The worker performs one POST through the fixed-host shared transport; no redirect or arbitrary-host setting was added. Existing framing, MIME, encoding and body limits remain shared with status GET. The new request body is bounded by validated field lengths and fits the worker input cap.

Independent execution: four creation tests and six existing status transport tests passed normally and with Python -O. A separate integration probe invokes the public create boundary, a real isolated Python worker and a real loopback HTTP server, replacing only the HTTPS connection factory inside that test worker. Success returns the exact original receipt bytes; an HTTP 502 and a server that receives POST then closes without responding both yield CreationUnknown. Each case observes exactly one POST. commands.json and raw outputs preserve these results.

No new blocking counterexample was found. Tests exercise parsing and process/HTTP behavior, not a real TLS handshake, OIDC issuance/validation, artifact provenance or GitHub authorization. The fixture credentials are synthetic. No live Pages API operation occurred. The README correctly requires the caller's confirmed durable intent, publication lock, permissions and provenance gates before use, and persistence/reconciliation afterward. This module alone does not provide a complete publisher, current-publication proof or LKG authorization. The reviewer made no implementation edits.
